# Copy to .env in this directory (the project root, next to run_airon.py):
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Nothing in it is ever printed - startup lists the
# names it loaded, never the values.

# The conversational brain. Without this aiRon still sees, recognises,
# greets people and asks names; it just cannot hold a conversation.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Which model the conversational brain talks through. Optional - unset means
# claude-opus-5, which is the one aiRon's personality was written against.
# Set it to try another (claude-sonnet-5, claude-opus-4-8) and listen to
# what changes: how long the pause before it speaks is, and whether it still
# sounds like aiRon rather than an assistant.
#
# Not every model will do. aiRon asks for effort "low" to keep the pause
# short, and models that predate that setting - claude-haiku-4-5 among them -
# reject the request outright rather than ignoring it. Nor is a wrong model
# id caught at startup: aiRon comes up as normal, then goes quiet every time
# somebody speaks, with the reason in the log as "[brain] model call failed".
# AIRON_LLM_MODEL=claude-opus-5
